<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.km6.fpaidl"
    android:versionCode="1"
    android:versionName="1.0">

    <uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion="35" android:targetSdkVersion="35" />

    <!--
      Clears config_biometric_sensors.

      AuthService decides which fingerprint code path system_server uses from
      this array (frameworks/base .../biometrics/AuthService.java):

          new FingerprintSensorConfigurations(
                  !(hidlConfigStrings != null && hidlConfigStrings.length > 0));

      A non-empty array therefore forces the legacy HIDL branch, which wraps
      every sensor in HidlToAidlSensorAdapter and looks for a HIDL
      IBiometricsFingerprint daemon. On this GSI the array is populated by
      com.mediatek.frameworkresoverlay and android.auto_generated_rro_product__,
      so the framework never takes the AIDL path even though the AIDL HAL is
      registered ; the resulting stuck FingerprintUpdateActiveUserClient is
      what hides the fingerprint entry in Settings.

      An empty array flips the decision to the AIDL branch.
    -->
    <overlay android:targetPackage="android" android:priority="100" android:isStatic="true" />

    <application android:hasCode="false" />
</manifest>
